# API contract lives in reactorlog/api

This repo is the SPA only. HTTP JSON shapes, routes, and DB schema are owned by
the sibling repo at `../api` (`github.com/reactorlog/api`).

Before changing fetch clients, parsers, stores, or pages under `src/sites/` or
`src/reactors/`:

1. Read `../api/internal/api/types.go` for JSON fields.
2. Read `../api/internal/api/handler.go` for routes and status codes.
3. If the change depends on persistence, skim `../api/migrations/sql/` and
   `../api/internal/api/store.go`.

Mirror the API in TypeScript. Parse `unknown` at the HTTP boundary. Do not add
OpenAPI, a shared package, or a second schema source unless the user asks.
Update colocated Vitest coverage when shapes or error mapping change.
